# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Text of the rewritten report (v5). Body = everything from '1. Introduction' to 'Appendices'."""

EXEC_SUMMARY = [
    "DNSE Securities is one of Vietnam's most effective acquirers of investors. It opened 518,514 accounts in 2025, 19 per cent of all accounts opened in the country, held 12.7 per cent of Vietnam's securities accounts at the end of the year and handled a quarter of derivatives brokerage in the second quarter of 2026. Zero-fee trading on the Entrade X app, no branch network and fast technology made this possible.",
    "The money has not followed the accounts. At 30 June 2026 DNSE held 2.3 to 3.5 per cent of the cash that investors keep at brokers, 1.4 to 1.8 per cent of margin lending and 0.6 to 0.8 per cent of the industry's quarterly pre-tax profit; each range runs from a press tally of all brokers to the sum of 42 filed statements. Only 5.7 per cent of accounts used any DNSE product in December 2025, and customer assets per account fell 9.5 per cent in 2025 while all three exchange indices rose. The gap is specific to DNSE. VPS, which has no parent bank, lends five times as much per account, and TCBS, which is also zero-fee and online, lends twelve times as much, with about a third of its customers trading each month.",
    "The income statement shows the cost. Operating revenue rose 3.2 times between 2022 and 2025, while pre-tax profit excluding proprietary trading stayed between VND 128 and 221 billion a year. In the first half of 2026 each extra VND 100 of core revenue came with VND 102 of extra cost. The filings show where it went: 52 per cent to funding, 42 per cent to direct brokerage cost and only 6 per cent to administration, which includes staff and technology. Brokerage has cost more than it earned for 16 consecutive quarters, and DNSE's brokerage loss in the first half of 2026 was the largest among 42 brokers. DNSE's cost of funds is in line with bank-owned peers. What is unusual is that 38 per cent of its assets sit in term deposits and bonds, 93 per cent of them pledged to banks, that earn about what they cost, while margin lending, its widest margin, uses 116 per cent of equity against a 200 per cent ceiling. The constraint is customer money, not capital or technology.",
    "Two causes are measured. DNSE's idle-cash account pays a typical customer 2.1 to 2.3 per cent, against 6.0 per cent at TCBS for the same balance from VND 5 million, and derivatives build market share without building balances at the broker. Two more are hypotheses for Round 3: reward-driven sign-ups, which dominate the most-endorsed complaints, and targets that reward acquisition rather than balances. Conditions raise the stakes. Deposit rates rose about 2.5 points in 2026, cash at brokers fell by more than a third in three quarters, and bank-owned brokers supplied more than half of the industry's lending growth in the second quarter.",
    "The priority problem is therefore the balance gap: accounts that are opened but never funded with meaningful savings. It ranks first of seven candidate problems on scale, urgency, strategic relevance, strength of evidence and DNSE's control. Reaching the 2026 profit plan from lending would need a loan book 2.3 times the current one.",
    "The recommended direction is Payday Portfolio, a salary-linked savings-to-investing layer for salaried adults of roughly 22 to 40, starting with working customers already in DNSE's base. It moves money on payday through ZaloPay and bank open interfaces, pays a market-linked yield through a partner bank or money market fund, ladders savings into bond funds, Trứng Vàng bonds and VN30 exchange-traded funds, and allows opt-in use of the portfolio as margin collateral. A trust layer removes the closure fee, pays rewards on funding rather than sign-up and reports the product to the regulator before launch. In the base case 150,000 savers would build VND 4.7 trillion of balances within 18 months, 2.4 times DNSE's investor cash today. Three quick wins run alongside: repricing the idle-cash account, reviewing the per-trade costs DNSE absorbs and reactivating dormant accounts.",
    "Round 3 should test seven assumptions before commitment, led by the distribution of balances by cohort, customers' response to the cash yield, the legal structure of the cash layer and enrolment in a 20,000-customer payday pilot.",
]

# Body blocks. ('h1', text) ('h2', text) ('p', text) ('pb', bold_lead, text) ('fig', key)
BODY = [
    ('h1', '1. Introduction'),
    ('h2', '1.1 DNSE and its business model'),
    ('p', "DNSE Securities began in 2007 as Dai Nam Securities and became a technology-led broker after Encapital acquired it in 2020 (CafeF, 2024c). Listed on HOSE since July 2024, it had total assets of VND 15.2 trillion and equity of VND 5.4 trillion at 30 June 2026 (DNSE, 2026a; Table A1). It sells only through the Entrade X app and website and offers lifetime zero-fee trading in listed shares (CafeF, 2024b). Revenue therefore comes from interest on margin loans, managed deal by deal through Margin Deal, derivatives brokerage, interest on term deposits and bonds held to maturity, and proprietary trading. Each depends on customers keeping money on the platform."),
    ('h2', '1.2 Market context'),
    ('p', "Vietnam had 11.9 million securities accounts at the end of 2025, against 7.3 million two years earlier, and individuals supply more than 90 per cent of trading value (Vietnam Securities Depository and Clearing Corporation [VSDC], 2026; Dân trí, 2026b). With TCBS, MBS, Pinetree and DNSE all offering zero-fee trading, commissions no longer separate brokers (CafeF, 2024b). Profit comes from lending, which earned securities firms VND 12.2 trillion in the second quarter of 2026 against VND 3.7 trillion from brokerage (Vietstock, 2026h)."),
    ('h2', '1.3 Business area and question'),
    ('p', "This report asks how DNSE can turn a large account base into funded customer relationships, and which savers it should target first. It asks where between sign-up and profit value is lost, measured against the market and named peers, why it is lost, and which response creates most value within DNSE's capabilities, funding and regulatory limits. Investment banking, proprietary trading strategy and new ventures are out of scope."),

    ('h1', '2. Findings of observations'),
    ('h2', '2.1 Evidence base and approach'),
    ('p', "The analysis combines eight datasets (Table A2). Its core is 395 line items of DNSE's filed statements from 2018 to mid-2026, pulled from Vietcap's data service and reconciled to the half-year statements reviewed by KPMG, with the same template for 41 other brokers. Market shares come from the original HOSE and HNX announcements, account totals from VSDC and customer indicators from DNSE's 2025 annual report. One cleaning rule set, applied equally to VPS and FPTS, removed loan advertising and referral farming from 867 DNSE Google Play reviews, leaving 670 (Table E1). Every share uses a denominator of the same date and definition; where a press tally and the sum of filed statements give different industry totals, both are reported. Hypotheses are labelled as such and reappear in the validation plan. The main limitation is the absence of customer-level data, so demographics and funnel stages are inferred (Table G3)."),
    ('h2', '2.2 Finding 1. DNSE wins accounts but not money'),
    ('p', "DNSE is one of Vietnam's most effective acquirers of customers. It opened 518,514 accounts in 2025, 19 per cent of the 2.68 million opened in the market, and held 12.7 per cent of all securities accounts at the end of the year (DNSE, 2026d; VSDC, 2026). Its share of derivatives brokerage rose from 4.0 per cent in the first quarter of 2024 to 25.4 per cent in the second quarter of 2026, second only to VPS (Hanoi Stock Exchange, 2026; Figure A1)."),
    ('p', "The picture reverses when money replaces registration as the measure (Figure 1). In the second quarter of 2026 DNSE handled 2.9 per cent of listed-share brokerage on HNX and stayed outside the HOSE top ten. At 30 June 2026 it held 2.3 to 3.5 per cent of investor cash at brokers, 1.4 to 1.8 per cent of margin lending and 0.6 to 0.8 per cent of quarterly industry pre-tax profit. An average DNSE account therefore holds 0.18 to 0.27 times the cash, and borrows 0.11 to 0.14 times the loans, of an average account in the market (Figure A2)."),
    ('fig', 'shares'),
    ('p', "The gap widens as the base grows. Margin lending per account fell from VND 4.4 million at the end of 2023 to VND 3.7 million in June 2026, and cash per account fell to VND 1.15 million (Figure A3). Customer assets per account fell 9.5 per cent in 2025, to VND 35.3 million, in a year when the VN-Index rose 41 per cent, the UPCoM index 28 per cent and the HNX-Index 9 per cent (DNSE, 2026d). Only 85,739 customers, 5.7 per cent of accounts, used any DNSE product in December 2025, twice as many as a year earlier but still a very low base."),
    ('h2', '2.3 Finding 2. The gap is specific to DNSE'),
    ('p', "Three objections could explain the gap away: that every broker counts dormant accounts, that app-based zero-fee brokers attract only small savers, or that DNSE lacks a parent bank. Peers with similar account bases answer all three (Figure 2; Table A3). VPS, a retail broker without a parent bank, lends VND 20.2 million per account, more than five times DNSE's VND 3.7 million. TCBS, also zero-fee with 99 per cent of accounts opened online, lends VND 42.9 million per account, and about 34 per cent of its customers traded on its app in December 2025, against 5.7 per cent of DNSE accounts using any product (TCBS, 2026c; Table D2). Second-quarter pre-tax profit per account was VND 57,000 at DNSE and VND 0.9 to 1.7 million at VPS, VPBankS and TCBS. Account counts differ in date, but not enough to close gaps of this size."),
    ('fig', 'peers'),
    ('p', "Customer reviews place the problem at the start of the relationship. Since March 2023, 5.6 per cent of DNSE's cleaned Google Play reviews concern sign-up bonuses or rewards, against 0.7 per cent for VPS and none for FPTS. The most-endorsed complaints, from June 2025, say that a VND 100,000 sign-up reward required a VND 2 million deposit and that closing an account cost VND 100,000 (Figure A5; Table E5). Deception, bonus terms and closure appear in 24 per cent of negative reviews but attract 43 per cent of their helpful votes (Figure A4). Crashes and login failures are more common but do not set DNSE apart, since its Google Play rating is above those of VPS and FPTS."),
    ('h2', '2.4 Finding 3. Revenue grows while core profit stands still'),
    ('p', "Operating revenue rose 3.2 times, from VND 452 billion in 2022 to VND 1,458 billion in 2025 (Figure A6). Pre-tax profit excluding proprietary trading stayed between VND 128 and 221 billion a year (Figure 3). The two years of strong reported growth, 2023 and 2025, rested on trading gains of VND 158 and 146 billion."),
    ('fig', 'core'),
    ('p', "In the first half of 2026 core revenue rose by VND 285 billion on a year earlier and core costs by VND 289 billion, so each extra VND 100 of core revenue brought about VND 102 of extra cost; including trading losses, pre-tax profit fell 29 per cent (Figure A7). By mid-year DNSE had delivered 20 per cent of its 2026 pre-tax profit target of VND 550 billion (Vietstock, 2026b), and its annualised return on equity of 3.8 per cent was below the 6.8 per cent paid on a 12-month deposit at a state-owned bank (VietnamNet, 2026)."),
    ('h2', '2.5 Finding 4. Brokerage and funding absorb the growth'),
    ('p', "The filings show where the extra cost went (Table A4). Of the VND 289 billion rise in core costs in the first half of 2026, funding took 52 per cent, direct brokerage cost 42 per cent and administration, which includes staff, outsourced services and technology, 6 per cent. Comparing 2025 with 2024 gives the same picture: brokerage 52, funding 40 and administration 5 per cent. Technology spending is not what absorbs revenue growth; fixed assets, including leased equipment, are 1 per cent of total assets."),
    ('p', "Brokerage is the first source. Its direct cost has exceeded brokerage revenue in each of the 16 quarters since the third quarter of 2022, with a cumulative shortfall of VND 190 billion (Figure 4). The cost moves with revenue, which covered 78 to 92 per cent of it in each of the last eight quarters, so it behaves as a per-trade cost, not a fixed investment. In the first half of 2026 DNSE lost VND 44.5 billion on brokerage after direct costs, the largest loss among 42 brokers with filed statements and 2.6 times the next, while the industry earned VND 1.5 trillion (Table A5). The notes do not split this cost, but DNSE pays exchange fees on free share trades and has paid derivatives margin fees for customers since May 2025 (Vietstock, 2025b)."),
    ('fig', 'brokerage'),
    ('p', "Funding is the second source. Average borrowings rose 43 per cent and the estimated cost of funds rose from 4.6 to 6.3 per cent between the first halves of 2025 and 2026 (Figure A8). The rate itself is normal: on the same method TCBS paid 7.8 per cent in the second quarter of 2026, VPBankS and MBS 6.8 per cent and VPS, which has no parent bank, 5.1 per cent, against DNSE's 6.5 per cent (Table A6)."),
    ('h2', '2.6 Finding 5. Capital is not the constraint'),
    ('p', "Margin loans were 116 per cent of DNSE's equity at 30 June 2026 against a regulatory ceiling of 200 per cent, leaving room for about VND 4.6 trillion of additional lending, and shareholders added VND 1.3 trillion in March 2026 (CafeF, 2026a). Lending is the widest margin: an 11.2 per cent yield in the first half of 2026 left a spread of about 4.9 points over the cost of funds, so each extra VND 1 trillion lent adds about VND 49 billion of pre-tax profit a year before credit losses. What limits lending is demand from customers with money."),
    ('p', "Meanwhile 38 per cent of total assets sits in term deposits and bonds held to maturity, against 1 to 22 per cent at eight large peers (Table A6), and 93 per cent of these assets were pledged to banks for DNSE's borrowing at 30 June 2026 (DNSE, 2026a, note 8(b)). They yielded about 6.0 per cent in the first half of 2026, close to the cost of the funds behind them (Figure A8), so they supply 23 per cent of revenue and almost no profit (Figure A9)."),

    ('h1', '3. Discussion and main analysis'),
    ('h2', '3.1 Why the money does not stay'),
    ('p', "A five-whys analysis links the symptom to DNSE's own design (Tables B1 and B2). Two causes are measured. The first is the price of the cash product: DNSE's idle-cash account pays a fixed 1.8 per cent, and 2.1 to 2.3 per cent to a customer with less than VND 500 million (DNSE, 2026b), while TCBS's iPower pays 6.0 per cent on the same balance from VND 5 million and banks' automatic-earning accounts paid 3.5 to 4.3 per cent in 2025 (TCBS, 2026a; DNSE, 2025; Figure B1). A saver has no financial reason to keep money at DNSE. The second is the product mix. Derivatives give DNSE its largest market share, but investors post margin at the clearing house, so the franchise builds activity, and brokerage losses, without building balances."),
    ('p', "Two further causes are hypotheses for Round 3: reward-driven intake, which would explain accounts that receive only the deposit a reward requires, and targets built on accounts, market share and order speed rather than balances, which would explain why no competitive savings product exists."),
    ('p', "Four alternative explanations were tested. The market cycle does not explain 2025, when every index rose and assets per account fell, and in 2026 DNSE's investor cash fell 38 per cent, in line with the industry (Figure B2). Capital is not the constraint, and the peer comparison controls for dormant accounts. The fourth, that DNSE acquires young customers now to monetise them later, cannot be rejected with public data, because new cohorts dilute per-account averages and active users doubled in 2025; cohort data, the first test in Section 4.4, would settle it."),
    ('h2', '3.2 Market and customer context'),
    ('p', "Conditions in 2026 raise the cost of the gap. Credit grew faster than deposits in 2025, banks raised 12-month deposit rates by about 2.5 points in 2026, and household deposits reached a record of more than VND 11 quadrillion in June (FiinRatings, 2026; VietnamNet, 2026; Vietstock, 2026i; Table B3). Cash at brokers fell by more than a third in three quarters (VnEconomy, 2026b), and bank-owned brokers supplied more than half of the growth in margin lending in the second quarter (Vietstock, 2026g). The pool is large: one tenth of one per cent of household deposits equals 5.6 times DNSE's investor cash (Table B4), and no independent digital broker yet offers salaried savers a competitive place for a monthly surplus (Table B5)."),
    ('p', "Findex data show that 37 per cent of Vietnamese adults receive wages into an account, with the largest formally saved surplus among working adults in the upper income groups (World Bank, 2025b; Appendix F). Young adults save into an account every month as often as older adults, but only 8 per cent save for old age, against 23 per cent of adults aged 25 and over. In a 2025 survey, 81 per cent of investors wanted professional advice and a third feared non-transparent fees (Nhân Dân, 2025; VnEconomy, 2025)."),
    ('h2', '3.3 Lessons from comparable firms abroad'),
    ('p', "Zero-fee brokers abroad met the same problem earlier and solved it by gathering assets (Table B6). Robinhood's growth after 2021 came from net deposits, USD 68 billion in 2025, helped by retirement accounts and a higher cash yield (Robinhood Markets, 2026), and Trade Republic passed the central bank rate to customers and automated savings plans, reaching more than EUR 150 billion of assets (Trade Republic, 2025). Vietnamese securities firms cannot take deposits, so DNSE must gather balances through partners (Table B7)."),
    ('h2', '3.4 Target market, priority problem and problem statement'),
    ('p', "Five candidate markets were scored on six weighted criteria (Table B8). Salaried mass-affluent adults rank first under both weighted and equal scores: they hold the formally saved surplus, earn monthly income and are partly in DNSE's base already. Young first-time investors remain DNSE's strongest franchise but its weakest source of balances, so the scope is salaried customers of roughly 22 to 40, including Gen Z customers once they start work, in their first 90 days on the platform (Table B9)."),
    ('p', "Seven candidate problems were compared on scale, urgency, strategic relevance, data support and control (Table B10). The balance gap ranks first under both weightings; the trust deficit ranks second and becomes a condition within the solution, and loss-making brokerage, reliance on trading gains and funding cost are partly its symptoms. Reaching the 2026 profit plan from lending at the current spread would need a loan book 2.3 times today's, backed by about 2.5 times the customer assets DNSE held at the end of 2025 (Figure B3)."),
    ('pb', 'Problem statement.', "DNSE opens nearly one in five of Vietnam's new securities accounts but holds 2.3 to 3.5 per cent of investor cash and 1.4 to 1.8 per cent of margin lending. It converts sign-ups into funded, retained relationships at a low rate, above all in the first 90 days, because its incentives reward opening accounts and its products give salaried customers no competitive, trusted reason to keep money on the platform. As a result, core profit has not grown since 2022 while revenue tripled (Table B11)."),
    ('h2', '3.5 Strategic alternatives'),
    ('p', "Six responses were scored on six weighted criteria (Table B12), and Payday Portfolio, a salary-linked savings-to-investing layer, ranks first. Continuing acquisition-led growth adds accounts from the segment with the least money. A derivatives-to-shares bridge waits for same-day trading, possibly until 2028 (Người Quan sát, 2026), and deepens exposure to the activity penalised in August 2026. An advisory tier needs advisers DNSE deliberately avoided, a bank or e-wallet alliance works better as a channel than as a strategy, and reintroducing fees would break the zero-fee promise. Three quick wins should run alongside: repricing the idle-cash account, reviewing the per-trade costs DNSE absorbs and reactivating dormant accounts."),

    ('h1', '4. Recommendations'),
    ('h2', '4.1 The preliminary recommendation'),
    ('p', "DNSE should build Payday Portfolio, a savings tab in Entrade X, separate from the trading screens, that turns a customer's monthly surplus into a growing balance (Figure B4). It targets salaried adults of roughly 22 to 40, starting with DNSE's own low-balance accounts held by working customers, and acts in the first 90 days and on each payday after them."),
    ('pb', 'Salary link.', "On payday a fixed amount chosen by the customer moves from a bank account or ZaloPay wallet to DNSE, through ZaloPay, a partner since 2023, or a standing order today, and through the open banking interfaces banks must support by March 2027 (Thanh Niên, 2023; State Bank of Vietnam, 2024)."),
    ('pb', 'Cash layer.', "Money earns a market-linked return through a sweep into a partner bank deposit or a licensed money market fund. The partner pays the yield and DNSE earns a distribution fee, so DNSE takes no deposits, and the yield does not depend on trading."),
    ('pb', 'Ladder.', "Goal rules split the balance between bond funds, the existing Trứng Vàng bonds from VND 1 million and VN30 exchange-traded funds, each shown with a realistic range of returns."),
    ('pb', 'Optional collateral.', "After a suitability check, part of the portfolio may back Margin Deal loans at conservative ratios; leverage is never the default."),
    ('pb', 'Trust layer.', "The closure fee is removed, rewards are paid only on money that stays, terms, uptime and onboarding success are published, onboarding moves to the VNeID platform, and the product is reported to the State Securities Commission before launch, once the control gaps found by the August 2026 penalty are closed (Market Times, 2026). Tables B13 and B14 set out the journey and the evidence."),
    ('h2', '4.2 Value logic and expected outcomes'),
    ('p', "Value comes in four ways, in order of certainty: retaining money that is already leaving, distribution fees on balances, lending against balances at a 4.9-point spread, and cheaper growth, since the first wave comes from accounts DNSE has already paid to acquire. In the base case, 150,000 savers, about one in eleven accounts, contribute VND 2.5 million a month and keep 70 per cent on the platform. After 18 months the layer would hold VND 4.7 trillion, 2.4 times DNSE's investor cash today, and earn about VND 72 billion a year (Table B15; Figure B5). It rebuilds the balance base for 2027 and 2028 but will not rescue the 2026 plan."),
    ('h2', '4.3 Feasibility and risks'),
    ('p', "The building blocks already exist (Table B16). Four risks matter most. On price, a competitive yield could cost more than it earns; a 3-point bonus paid by DNSE on all existing investor cash would cost about VND 59 billion a year, so any bonus applies to new contributions only. On regulation, a structure deemed deposit-taking would be refused, so sweep and fund routes are preferred. On conduct, collateral use is opt-in and capped. On execution, a savings product that fails on payday would destroy trust, so reliability targets are a launch condition."),
    ('h2', '4.4 Validation direction'),
    ('p', "Seven assumptions must be tested before commitment (Table B17), led by the distribution of balances by cohort, customers' response to the cash yield in a randomised test, the legal structure of the cash layer and a 20,000-customer payday pilot, which should reach 25 per cent enrolment within 60 days with 70 per cent of contributions kept at 90 days. The legal structure is settled first and gates the pilot (Figure B6). The main success measure is the funded-account rate, the share of accounts holding at least VND 5 million for 30 consecutive days."),

    ('h1', '5. Conclusion'),
    ('p', "DNSE has solved the hardest problem for a new broker, getting noticed: it opens nearly one in five new accounts in Vietnam and handles a quarter of derivatives brokerage. It has not solved the problem that decides profit, getting customers to keep money with it. Its accounts hold a fraction of the market's cash and loans, its core profit has not grown since 2022, and each extra unit of revenue now brings as much extra cost, mostly per-trade brokerage cost and funding. The constraint is the product and its incentives, which Payday Portfolio changes. Round 3 should begin by measuring how many of DNSE's accounts are funded today."),
]

